glossary_Skill: "Use the most common word for an activated ability in your language's game industry."
glossary_Damage: "The standard combat term for damage."
glossary_Critical_Strike: "Keep the same wording used for critical hits in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Multiplier: "The standard term for multiplicative bonuses."
glossary_Defense: "Keep the same wording used for defense in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Buff: "Keep the same wording used for buff in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Life: "Keep the same wording used for health/life in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Mana: "Keep the same wording used for mana in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Mob: "Keep the same wording used for mob/enemy in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Aegis_Charge: "This is the charge that increases life, maximum life and defense."
glossary_Focus_Charge: "This is the charge that increases damage, critical strike chance and critical strike damage."
glossary_Haste_Charge: "This is the charge that increases attack speed, movement speed and projectile speed."
glossary_Summon: "Keep the same wording used for summons in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Apply: "The same as Inflict"
glossary_Inflict: "The same as Apply"
glossary_knockback: "Keep the same wording used for knockback in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_Increased: "In context of increasing something, this is an addictive change."
glossary_Increased_Damage: "An additive damage bonus: every 'increased' damage bonus is added together first, then applied to the base damage once. Example: with two sources of 10% increased damage, 100 base damage becomes 120 (100 x (1 + 0.10 + 0.10)). Must be worded differently from 'more damage'."
glossary_Regeneration: "Keep the same wording used for regeneration in Terraria's official translation."
glossary_More: "In context of increasing something, this is a multiplicative change."
glossary_More_Damage: "A multiplicative damage bonus: every 'more' damage bonus is applied separately, after all 'increased' damage bonuses are added up. Example: with two sources of 10% more damage, 100 base damage becomes 121 (100 x 1.10 x 1.10). Must be worded differently from 'increased damage'."